01:43:29 said  I've built a new standalone version of the word processor. It never connects to the internet and has no scanning (TWAIN) or sharing features. The build succeeds, Craft Anything's comparison check now passes, and six automatic tests of typing and page layout pass. I also looked at a sample document on screen to confirm the text draws correctly.
01:43:29 said  **What's in it:**
01:43:29 said  - The original's menu order (File, Edit, View, Create, Page, Text, Window, Help), with all the internet, scanning and team-sharing commands taken out.
01:43:29 said  - A single row of new flat, modern icons.
01:43:29 said  - Documents open in tabs instead of separate windows.
01:43:29 said  - Real pages with margins, a ruler, headers and footers, and page numbers.
01:43:29 said  - Text styles, fonts, colours, highlighting, alignment, bullets and numbering.
01:43:29 said  - Find & Replace with the original's four match options (whole words, starting with, ending with, containing), plus a word count.
01:43:29 said  - The original's own list of 170 auto-corrections (for example "teh" becomes "the").
01:43:29 said  - A recovery copy saved every 10 minutes, kept only on this computer.
01:43:29 said  - Light and dark themes.
01:43:29 said  As you asked, it always opens at 100% zoom, lets you zoom from 25% to 200%, and starts in 12-point Times New Roman.
01:43:29 said  **What's different or missing:**
01:43:29 said  - **Name:** it's called "Scribe Pro". The question about using the "Word Pro" name got no answer, and that name is a trademark.
01:43:29 said  - **Printing and spell checking aren't included yet.** For now you can save as Rich Text and print from another program.
01:43:29 said  - **Old files:** it saves its own document files and Rich Text or plain text files, but can't open the old program's own document files. Save those as Rich Text in the old program first.
01:43:29 said  - **Estimated details:** I couldn't find the original's exact list of font sizes, or how much F4 grows text, so those are my best guesses.
01:43:30 said  A good next request would be "add printing and a spell checker that works offline".
